                <pb facs="0510" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg406"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">362.1163 Watch Tower/6: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Germany (Gordon)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-04-27T18:00:00-05:00">April 27, 1933—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>46. The Watch Tower Bible and Tract Society, an American corporation, states that
                    it has been informed that the German Government has forcibly taken possession of
                    the Society’s property at Magdeburg, consisting of a printing and bookbinding
                    establishment and real estate valued at $600,000, and that the German
                    authorities have confiscated its books and other personal property.</p>
                <p>Please investigate with a view to lending appropriate assistance, and submit a
                    telegraphic report on the situation. The Society’s representative in Germany is
                    Paul Balzereit, Magdeburg.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
